**Plan, nothing changed yet.**

One catch: "same data" is ambiguous. `toTable` drops `owner` and `slow` on purpose. `buildRows()` keeps both. I'd have `--json` print the full row, since JSON has no width limit, and say so.

Two edits:

```js
// src/format.js
function toJson(rows) { return JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2); }
module.exports = { toTable, toJson, COLUMNS };

// src/cli.js  — main(argv)
const args = argv.filter((a) => a !== '--json');
const json = argv.includes('--json');
if (args[0] !== 'report') { ... }
process.stdout.write((json ? toJson : toTable)(buildRows()) + '\n');
```

`USAGE` becomes `usage: cli.js report [--json]`. Row order stays slowest first. No test files exist, so I would check by running both forms.

Next: say if `--json` should carry `owner` and `slow`, then I write it.
